<content>
<callout icon="🎯" color="blue_bg">
	Call reviews happen weekly. Every rep who wants to improve listens to their own calls. The best closers review their calls more than anyone else.
</callout>
**Recordings folder:** being created with the Master Tracking Drive — link drops here when live.
**Reference call in the meantime:** Brady closing a real prospect — [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uLk2JMC-SZ-Xqrmaum4YlOKgMQe3Vf82/view](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uLk2JMC-SZ-Xqrmaum4YlOKgMQe3Vf82/view) (internal training only, never send to prospects). Listen for how he prices up and how he talks about placement without ever saying "guaranteed."
### Recording Requirements
- All calls must be recorded (with prospect consent verbally stated at start of call)
- Upload to the drive folder within 24 hours of the call
- Label as: \[DATE\] — \[LEAD NAME\] — \[OUTCOME\]
### What to Self-Review
- **Did you complete the Perspective Shift before pitching?**
- Did you get verbal commitment before presenting investment?
- Did you handle objections by re-anchoring to outcome, not dropping price?
- How long did rapport building take? Was it deep enough?
- Where did you lose the call? What would you do differently?
</content>
